The '''Oba Diah system''' was a [[star system]] located in the [[Kessel sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. It was located in grid square T-10 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]]<ref name="Appendix" /> and contained the [[planet]] [[Oba Diah]].<ref name="The Lost One" />

{{System-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Oba Diah system was first identified in "[[Star Systems of the Galaxy]]," an appendix published alongside the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]] on [[StarWars.com]]<ref name="Appendix" /> on [[June 24]], [[2025]]. Both were written by [[Jason Fry]].<ref name="Substack">{{Substack|subdomain=jasonfry|url=p/about-that-new-star-wars-galaxy-map|text=About That New Star Wars Galaxy Map&hellip;|name=[[Jason Fry]]|username=jasonfry|date=2025-06-24}}</ref> ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'' places Oba Diah in the [[Kessel system]],<ref name="Official Guide" /> while ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]'' places it in its own system on the [[Pabol Sleheyron]].<ref name="Tales">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> However, later maps created by [[Christopher Ibbitt]] and [[Jason Fry]], such as the one in ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]'' and the [[2025]] [[Star Wars Galaxy Map|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]], and its "[[Star Systems of the Galaxy]]" appendix, instead move Oba Diah to along the [[Triellus Trade Route]].<ref name="Map" />

